From 0d132d3c792c1565c45549ee1f18ba3fd8570564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Cell PM2 (claude-opus-5-5)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:29:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B70-0031: KV offload CPU->GPU loads DMA straight from the
 pinned pool (no staging)

vllm-xpu-kernels swap_blocks_batch stages every CPU->GPU batch through one
pinned buffer of the batch total, taken from torch XPU CachingHostAllocator,
even though the offload pool is already pinned. With
pinned_max_cached_size_mb:1024 that buffer is rounded to a power of two and
cached forever: one block per concurrently outstanding load per size class.
Under CPU-tier-heavy traffic (kvreplay, 6 sessions, kv128) worker xe host
memory grew 64 MiB + 0.5 + 1 + 1 GiB per rank and ramguard stopped both
engines (obs 1f25ce6d).

With B70_OFFLOAD_H2D_DIRECT=1 the CPU->GPU handler maps each descriptor back
to (storage, offset), merges descriptors contiguous on both sides, and issues
non_blocking torch copies on the transfer stream. torch-xpu-ops copies a
pinned source with a direct q.memcpy + record_event on the pool block (no
staging). The manager keeps a loading chunk ref_cnt > 0 until its job
finishes, so no snapshot is needed (same assumption as CUDA
cuMemcpyBatchAsync). A descriptor outside its segment raises instead of
copying. GPU->CPU stores are unchanged (already direct). Unset/0 = upstream.

One-time log lines per worker: "B70-0031: CPU->GPU KV loads copy directly
from the pinned offload pool (...)" at init, and "B70-0031: first direct
CPU->GPU load: N descriptors -> M copies" on the first load.
---
 vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/gpu_worker.py | 154 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 154 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/gpu_worker.py b/vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/gpu_worker.py
index b753cf9..6b1236c 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/gpu_worker.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/gpu_worker.py
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
